FloppyBridge driver sources: two buffered-path fixes.

Applied to sources/src/floppybridge/ after the pristine RobSmithDev/FloppyDriveBridge
sources are copied in, alongside the portability patch. Behavioural, not a
portability fix, so it lives in its own file.

HISTORY. Until 2026-09-02 this patch also carried the streaming-read hooks
(admBeginFluxStream / admPumpFluxStream / admEndFluxStream on GreaseWeazleInterface,
and LinearExtractor::bitsWritten) that supported our AdmStreamingBridge, the
streaming Greaseweazle driver. That driver never beat the buffered Greaseweazle
driver and was removed (docs/floppy.md section 12, docs/floppy-xcopy-buffered.md
section 8g); the hooks went with it. What remains are the two fixes to upstream's
buffered path, which the Greaseweazle reference and driver 4 (XCopy buffered)
depend on.

FIXES TO THE BUFFERED PATH

1. Do not drain an aborted capture one byte at a time. Once abortReadStreaming()
   sets m_shouldAbortReading, upstream switches the read to a single byte per
   iteration, so cancelling drains the rest of a ~259ms flux stream a byte at a
   time over USB serial while a queued seek waits. The zero-terminator scan in the
   else branch already handles a full buffer, and bytesAvailable is bounded by
   getBytesWaiting(). MEASURED WORTH ~2 FRAMES on its own: side-0 25.4 -> 23.5,
   side-1 11.5 -> 10.3, with no other change.

2. Keep the track cache across a guest reset. qcResetDrive called resetMFMCache(),
   so anything captured while the machine sat idle was discarded the moment the
   disk was booted. A guest reset does not change the platter. Media changes still
   clear the cache in the disk-change handler. Gated on m_shouldAutoCache.

NEGATIVE RESULTS, recorded so they are not retried: releasing the drive to read
ahead once the guest has a usable 'current' made things WORSE (25.4 -> 30.8);
reordering which track gets cached changed nothing, because
handleBackgroundCaching() barely runs during a load.

Regenerated with `git diff --no-index` from pre/post copies - the hunk counts are
machine made, not hand edited (docs/floppy-xcopy.md section 7 on why that matters).

--- a/sources/src/floppybridge/CommonBridgeTemplate.cpp
+++ b/sources/src/floppybridge/CommonBridgeTemplate.cpp
@@ -1153,7 +1153,21 @@ void CommonBridgeTemplate::processCommand(const QueueInfo& info) {
 		m_isMotorRunning = false;		
 		m_readLoops = 0;
 		m_lastSeek = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
-		resetMFMCache();
+		// ADM: a guest reset does not change the platter, so with caching on keep the
+		// captured tracks and reset only the streaming state. Media changes still clear
+		// the cache in the disk-change handler. No effect when caching is off.
+		if (m_shouldAutoCache) {
+			resetWriteBuffer();
+			m_pll.reset();
+			{
+				std::lock_guard lockbuff(m_readBufferAvailableLock);
+				m_readBufferAvailable = false;
+			}
+			m_writePending = false;
+			m_writeComplete = false;
+			m_lastWroteTo = -1;
+		}
+		else resetMFMCache();
 		// Get some real disk status values
 		if (supportsDiskChange()) {
 			m_diskInDrive = getDiskChangeStatus(true);
